## 4. Key Optimizations Detailed

### 🕹️ 1. Camera & Controls Optimization
- Converted per-frame allocations inside `useFrame` in `MuseumControls.jsx` to reusable static vectors (`_moveVector`, `_forward`, `_side`).
- Added distance-squared thresholding (`distSq > 0.0625`) and time-gating (`150ms`) before notifying the parent `onCameraMove`.

### 📦 2. GLB Caching & Normalization
- Pre-calculated and memoized model bounding boxes inside `AutoFitModel.jsx` via `normalizedCache`.
- Re-enabled native Three.js GPU frustum culling (`child.frustumCulled = true`) so meshes outside the camera frustum are automatically skipped by the WebGL renderer.

### 🖼️ 3. Renderer & Canvas Configuration
- Configured Canvas DPR limits: `dpr={isArMode ? [1, 1.2] : [1, 1.5]}`.
- Added WebGL context flags: `powerPreference: "high-performance"`, `stencil: false`, `preserveDrawingBuffer: true`.

### 📱 4. Mobile AR-Specific Performance
- In Mobile WebXR AR mode, only the single `selectedArtifact` is loaded into memory.
- Dynamic shadows and post-processing are disabled in AR mode to keep frame rates steady on mobile GPUs.

